      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": 9,
        "title": "Another common thing in English are the interrogative words which can be used in any tense. Check out the following examples and how to identify them.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Another common thing in English are the interrogative words which can be used in any tense. Check out the following examples and how to identify them.",
          "Word Information Sample Questions 1 Who People Who sometimes goes to the beach on weekends? 2 How Often Regularity How often does Peter go to the beach on weekends? 3 How Manner/Ways How does Peter sometimes go to the beach on weekends? 4 What Actions/Objects What does Peter do on weekends because he loves it? 5 Where Places Where does Peter sometimes go on weekends? 6 When Time When does Peter go to the beach? 7 Why Reasons/Explanations Why does Peter sometimes go to the beach on weekends?",
          "Peter sometimes goes to the beach on weekends by car because he loves it. Who How often What Where When How Why",
          "Every interrogative word asks for specific information; look at the chart:",
          "Bonus: I normally go to class with Jane. Who do you normally go to class with?"
        ],
