      {
        "number": 13,
        "internalPageId": 13,
        "title": "Tom wakes up at 5 AM every day. He takes a shower and after that, he has breakfast. At 7:30 AM, he goes out to go to work and he arrives to his job at 8:00 AM. He is a lawyer, so he is sometimes in the office but he is usually at the supreme court. He always finishes work after 5:00 PM and he normally gets home at 8:00 PM. 1. Tom never wakes up at 6 AM. (T) (F) 2. He has breakfast first. (T) (F) 3. He starts work at 7 AM. (T) (F) 4. He is usually at court. (T) (F) 5. He is normally at home at 8 PM. (T) (F)",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Tom wakes up at 5 AM every day. He takes a shower and after that, he has breakfast. At 7:30 AM, he goes out to go to work and he arrives to his job at 8:00 AM. He is a lawyer, so he is sometimes in the office but he is usually at the supreme court. He always finishes work after 5:00 PM and he normally gets home at 8:00 PM. 1. Tom never wakes up at 6 AM. (T) (F) 2. He has breakfast first. (T) (F) 3. He starts work at 7 AM. (T) (F) 4. He is usually at court. (T) (F) 5. He is normally at home at 8 PM. (T) (F)",
          "A. Read the following paragraph and state if the sentences are true (T) or False (F). After that, read the paragraph aloud for your teacher."
        ],
        "links": [],
